le internally to store and retrieve elements efficiently.Does not allow duplicate values. Does not maintain insertion order. Uses hashing to store elements and provide fast search, insertion, and deletion operations.132. What is LinkedHashSet in Java Collections Framework?The LinkedHashSet is an ordered version of Hashset maintained by a doubly-linked List across all the elements. It is very helpful when iteration order is needed. During Iteration in LinkedHashSet, elements are returned in the same order they are inserted.Syntax:LinkedHashSet<E> hs = new LinkedHashSet<E>();
